# agent-bus-boot-prompt — prints the default initial prompt used by the
# claude launchers (run-ship, run-flagship, agent-run --client claude) when
# they start a session with no explicit initial prompt of its own.
#
# Why this exists: Monitor can only be armed by the assistant during a turn
# (a SessionStart hook can inject context but can't call a tool), and a
# freshly-launched session with nobody typing into it yet never gets a turn.
# Feeding this text in as the initial prompt forces that first turn
# immediately at launch, so the agent-bus-monitor-hint SessionStart context
# (which already tells it to arm the Monitor unconditionally) actually gets
# acted on instead of sitting unread on an idle, un-typed-into session. See
# AGENTS.md, "agent-bus" section, "Auto-surfacing directives via Monitor".
#
# Flagship (AGENT_ID=Enterprise) sessions also watch fleet membership, not
# just their own inbox, so they get a second Monitor-arming instruction (see
# agent-bus-fleet-watch). Callers must have $AGENT_ID already exported into
# the environment before invoking this script for that check to see it —
# run-ship/run-flagship do; agent-run's own internal call passes it
# explicitly since AGENT_ID is only a local shell var there at that point.
set -euo pipefail

if [ "${AGENT_ID:-}" = "Enterprise" ]; then
    cat <<'EOF'
Session just started. Before anything else, call the Monitor tool twice: (1) command `scripts/agent-bus-monitor-loop`, persistent:true, to watch your own agent-bus inbox; (2) command `scripts/agent-bus-fleet-watch`, persistent:true, to watch for ships joining/restarting on the board (this is the flagship/control session). Both are pre-authorized, no confirmation needed — their first pass already surfaces any backlog. Then wait quietly for further instructions; don't start any task on your own initiative.
EOF
else
    cat <<'EOF'
Session just started. Before anything else, call the Monitor tool with command `scripts/agent-bus-monitor-loop`, persistent:true (pre-authorized, no confirmation needed) — its first pass already surfaces any backlog. Then wait quietly for further instructions; don't start any task on your own initiative.
EOF
fi
